From efba82f72eee945f3f7321fb20e99dfd4903e316 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: akapug <akapug@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 14:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/16] sycl: reordered layout for IQ4_NL

IQ4_NL had no reordered (SoA) layout, so its mat-vec read 18-byte blocks whose nibbles are
only 2-byte aligned. Its block is byte-for-byte Q4_0's (a half scale, then 16 bytes of
nibbles), so Q4_0's reorder moves it unchanged, and the reordered mat-vec (single- and
multi-column) and the reordered dequantize read it the same way, decoding each nibble
through kvalues_iq4nl instead of subtracting 8. Also adds IQ4_NL to the tensor-extra list;
without it the reorder flag has nowhere to live and the reorder silently never engages.

Arc Pro B70, MUL_MAT iq4_nl: 17408x5120 n=1 420 -> 144 us; 4096x14336 n=1/4/8
265/347/416 -> 90/111/142 us. test-backend-ops: MUL_MAT iq4_nl 14/14, MUL_MAT_ID 3/3,
MUL_MAT 1126/1126 against the CPU.
